<p>U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio used a keynote address at the Munich Security Conference to tell European leaders that the United States and Europe “belong together.” He cast Washington as committed to the transatlantic relationship, while still pressing for changes that match President Trump’s approach to the alliance. Many European officials and analysts said his diplomatic tone was noticeably warmer than last year’s appearance by Vice President JD Vance, and the friendlier rhetoric drew applause in the room. Even so, Rubio’s remarks did not resolve the main policy tensions. European leaders said they welcomed the calmer language but stayed cautious, pointing to ongoing disagreements over who carries the security burden and to wider strains in U.S.-Europe ties. Rubio paired reassurance with criticism on issues such as migration and international institutions, and some coverage noted his warnings about “civilizational erasure” — a reminder that the administration’s core message has not fundamentally changed, even if the packaging has.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/NeZ8meVEUoS5AxRQKTVxthVaoz3b3Q36uDAlgr1nvhckgAGOubmhqioyq81HamoDvckgEpN_ioooF36opk0gGxIKznlzkIjFC3gD69SndqU7BeulwZZGkdbBgAzqvHEEPH3aLeWWZgZM5bWJCyBdWhociRmrYTllFem8Hg2AeyXiBmBx5v42qsER-mfPtb8fd_huwVMwTp_iopA6' alt='Secretary of State Marco Rubio speaking at the Munich Security Conference.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>NATO posture: U.S. Ambassador to NATO Matthew Whitaker said “Americans are not leaving” Europe, but argued Europe should shoulder more of the conventional-defense burden so the U.S. can free up capacity for other regions.</li><li>Greenland backdrop: Rubio’s outreach came as Europe remains unsettled by President Trump’s stated ambitions to seize Greenland, an autonomous territory of Denmark, a NATO and EU member.</li><li>Trade frictions backdrop: Several reports noted Rubio spoke amid broader U.S.-Europe strains, including the Trump administration’s trade fight with many European allies.</li><li>Ukraine track: Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty reported Rubio reassured President Volodymyr Zelenskyy of U.S. commitment, while warning that any path toward ending the war could involve “hard” concessions.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Johann Wadephul: Dawn reported that Wadephul praised Rubio for focusing on what Europe and America had achieved together in the past, while European officials more broadly stressed that uncertainties and differences remained. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1973337/europe-gives-cautious-welcome-to-rubios-warmer-tone'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Finland’s President Alexander Stubb: He said the tone from U.S. officials is calmer, but warned that American foreign policy has changed. He described a mix of “very MAGA” ideology and “America First” priorities. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/finland-president-alexander-stubb-us-shift-in-tone-not-substance/'>POLITICO Europe</a>)</li><li>European leaders at the conference: The New York Times reported that even officials who welcomed Rubio’s less confrontational style said they still lacked clarity on what it would mean in practice — including U.S. expectations on European defense spending and how Washington might handle core security questions like troop posture and the Ukraine war. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/14/world/europe/europe-reaction-rubio.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>U.S. Department of State (Rubio): Rubio framed disagreements as rooted in U.S. concern for Europe and argued the two sides are linked “spiritually” and “culturally,” while urging Europe to join a U.S.-led “renewal.” (<a href='https://time.com/7378722/rubio-europe-speech-us-trump/'>Time</a>)</li><li>European security commentators: Several outlets said Rubio’s warmer presentation did little to change the underlying European calculation that Washington’s priorities are shifting. That has left governments planning around higher defense spending and greater self-reliance, even as U.S. officials insist the alliance will endure. (<a href='https://www.economist.com/europe/2026/02/14/america-offers-europe-warmer-words-but-a-deep-chill-remains'>The Economist</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Foreign-Policy/2026/0214/rubio-speech-munich-allies'>Rubio’s speech to European allies takes softer tone but keeps firm stance</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/02/14/world/munich-security-conference-rubio'>Live Updates: In Munich, Rubio Calls Europe a Friend but Says It Must Change</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1973337/europe-gives-cautious-welcome-to-rubios-warmer-tone'>Europe gives cautious welcome to Rubio’s warmer tone</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/02/14/nx-s1-5714465/rubios-words-reassure-europe-but-tensions-remain'>Rubio&#x27;s words reassure Europe, but tensions remain</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/94633f65-04c0-4cea-b682-98c17720eebc'>‘The best we can hope for’: Rubio’s Munich unity appeal fails to woo Europe</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/finland-president-alexander-stubb-us-shift-in-tone-not-substance/'>Europe’s Trump whisperer doesn’t buy US cuddly pivot</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/02/14/us-ambassador-nato-europe-munich-00782365'>US Ambassador to NATO: America is ‘not leaving’ Europe</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/2/14/rubio-at-munich-security-conference-us-wants-europe-to-be-strong'>Rubio at Munich Security Conference: US wants Europe to be ‘strong’</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/marco-rubio-donald-trump-european-union-munich-security-conference/'>Rubio calls for U.S. and Europe to &quot;revitalize an old friendship&quot;</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1r4rtcz/rubio_says_us_is_unsure_if_russia_is_serious/'>Rubio says US is unsure if Russia is serious about ending Ukraine war</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://time.com/7378722/rubio-europe-speech-us-trump/'>What We Learned From Marco Rubio’s Foreign Policy Speech to European Leaders</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/rubio-zelenskyy-ukraine-munich-russia-war/33678813.html'>Rubio Reassures Zelenskyy Of US Commitment, But Warns Of &#x27;Hard&#x27; Concessions</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/european-reaction-to-rubios-speech-on-transatlantic-ties-at-munich-security-conference'>European reaction to Rubio&#x27;s speech on transatlantic ties at Munich Security Conference</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/rubio-tries-to-reassure-skeptical-european-allies-but-follows-trumps-vision-for-a-reshaped-alliance'>Rubio tries to reassure skeptical European allies but pushes Trump&#x27;s vision for reshaped alliance</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.economist.com/europe/2026/02/14/america-offers-europe-warmer-words-but-a-deep-chill-remains'>America offers Europe warmer words, but a deep chill remains</a> - economist.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/rubio-expresses-desire-to-maintain-trans-atlantic-relations-despite-increasing-rift'>Rubio&#x27;s speech to European allies takes a softer tone but sticks to Trump&#x27;s firm stance</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2lrdq47149o'>Rubio says US and Europe &#x27;belong together&#x27; despite tensions</a> - bbc.com</li></ul>